Context: T139. Decision: report the real build version rather than pin a protocol-level constant — the MCP initialize serverInfo.version now comes from internal/buildinfo.Identity(), the same source as ohya version (T061), so the version string alone identifies the build (dev pseudo-version embeds commit+dirty; release builds carry the injected tag). The ldflags symbol moved main.releaseVersion -> github.com/nibzard/ohya/internal/buildinfo.ReleaseVersion (scripts/package.sh, ADR 0008, docs/performance.md updated); any external release tooling that sets the old symbol must move too. One intentional behavior delta: when debug.ReadBuildInfo fails, the linked release tag now still wins over the devel fallback (the old cmd/ohya code ignored it on that path). Verified by live stdio initialize probes on both a dev build (pseudo-version) and an ldflags-injected build (v0.2.1-test), plus TestInitializeReportsBuildVersion and the stdio e2e assertion.
